# A picture:  its own page on Wikipedia, if it has one, else an initial on a colour
A widget of its own, as no `ui-image` falls back on anything:  an initial shows until a picture comes, and stays if none does.
A species with no picture of its own takes the first of its people who has one:  Hutt, Jabba.

<spell-thing "portrait">
	<property "name" />
	<property "hue" />
	<property "shape" />
	<spell>
		- its "species" is a species
	</spell>
	<property "page">the wiki page whose id is its name</property>
	<property "initial">the first letter of its name</property>
	<property "picture">
		if its page and its page's fits and its page's thumbnail
			return its page's thumbnail's source
		if its species
			return its species' picture
		return ""
	</property>
	<draw>
		<segment class={"portrait " + its shape} style={"--hue: " + its hue} appearance="basic">
			<header class="initial">{its initial}</header>
			{draw its photo}
		</segment>
	</draw>
	<draw "photo" description="Waiting for it, or if Wikipedia can't be reached, the initial stays">
		<if its picture is not "">
			<image src={its picture} alt="" crop="top" />
		</if>
		while waiting:
			<space />
		if that fails:
			<space />
	</draw>
</spell-thing>
